  "notes": "{漏|も}らす means to let something escape or slip out, either physically or informationally.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {漏|も}れる (intransitive, something leaks out)\n\nMEANINGS:\n1. Physical leaking: {水|みず}を{漏|も}らす (to leak water)\n2. Information: {秘密|ひみつ}を{漏|も}らす (to divulge a secret)\n3. Omitting: {名前|なまえ}を{漏|も}らす (to leave out a name)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {秘密|ひみつ}を{漏|も}らす: to let slip a secret\n- {情報|じょうほう}を{漏|も}らす: to leak information\n- {本音|ほんね}を{漏|も}らす: to let one's true feelings slip\n- ため{息|いき}を{漏|も}らす: to let out a sigh",
